NOTICE — what the MIT grant in `LICENSE` covers, and what it does not
=====================================================================

This file is part of the licensing terms of this repository. `LICENSE` grants
MIT; this file states the boundary of that grant. Read them together.

It lives in a separate file for one mechanical reason, stated so it does not
look like an afterthought: GitHub classifies a repository's licence by matching
the text of `LICENSE` against known licences. Any text appended to the MIT
wording makes the match fail, and the repository is labelled "Other" — which
tells a reader nothing about what they may do. Keeping `LICENSE` as the exact
MIT text and the boundary here makes the grant legible to both a person and a
machine.


